  "Question": "The average weight of \\(6\\) boys is \\(150\\) pounds and the average weight of \\(4\\) girls is \\(120\\) pounds. The average weight of the \\(10\\) children is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(135\\) pounds",
    "B": "\\(137\\) pounds",
    "C": "\\(138\\) pounds",
    "D": "\\(140\\) pounds",
    "E": "\\(141\\) pounds"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "An average multiplied by the number of children gives their total weight. The boys therefore weigh \\(6\\cdot150=900\\) pounds altogether, and the girls weigh \\(4\\cdot120=480\\) pounds altogether.\n\nAdding these totals and dividing by all \\(10\\) children gives the combined average:\n\\[\n\\frac{900+480}{10}=\\frac{1380}{10}=138\\text{ pounds}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{138\\text{ pounds}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
